<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Android network security configuration.

Purpose:
Radio stations are discovered dynamically through the Radio Browser index.
Many legitimate stations still expose their stream over plain http rather than
https. On Android 9+ (API 28+) cleartext HTTP is blocked by default, which can
cause otherwise-valid stations to fail with UNABLE TO CONNECT.

Because station domains cannot be known in advance (the catalogue is
discovered at runtime), a per-domain cleartext allow-list is not practical for
this product. We therefore permit cleartext traffic at the app level.

Security scope:
* HTTPS remains preferred. This config only permits cleartext; it never
  downgrades an HTTPS stream, and it does not rewrite http to https or the
  reverse. Stations flagged HTTPS by the index are streamed over HTTPS.
* TLS certificate validation is NOT weakened. No trust-anchors override is
  present, so Android continues using the system CA store and rejects invalid
  or mis-issued certificates.
* The app's own API calls (Radio Browser index, Podcast Index, RSS feeds) all
  use hardcoded HTTPS base URLs and are unaffected.

If a future offline allow-list of known-good station domains ever becomes
available, this can be narrowed to those specific domains.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
